 "equipment_type": "VAV box controller",
 "applies_to": "ProLon VAV zone controllers (VC2000, C1050-VAV and related hardware) running VAV firmware 7.6.0.",
 "summary": "ProLon's VAV controller exposes its whole configuration (setpoints, PI tuning, damper and airflow settings, five configurable outputs, math functions) and its live network variables (zone temperature, setpoints, airflow, demand, outputs, occupancy) as Analog, Multi-state and Binary Values. The five outputs can each be assigned a function, so what Out1-Out5 do depends on the configuration.",
 "bacnet_transport": [],
 "firmware": "7.6.0",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Configuration objects (AV 20-115, MV 2-24, BV 6-31) carry no writable column in the profile; they are listed as writable configuration with the printed default and min/max. Network variables use the printed BACnet Writable column.",
  "Temperatures are printed in °C (units 62); BV 29 switches BACnet temperature units to °F.",
  "MV 21 has two printed rows: VC2000 analog input mode (1-7) and a bit-coded C1050 input profile (1-256).",
  "AV 71 and AV 72 (Group Weight 2/3) are printed with the object name GrpWght1, same as AV 70.",
  "Instances skip AV 101/103/104 in the configuration block (they are network variables) and BV 28/32 are network variables too.",
  "The profile does not say which BACnet data link (BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP) the controller uses; it only lists Net port and RJ45 port serial settings."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "VAV Controller Network Profile - BACnet Ver 7.6.0",
